        "editorial": "The reference rule does three things in order. If there is card debt, it pays it off first, because 20% a year beats any expected return. Until the buffer covers 3 months of essential costs, it saves. After that, it invests. A 2-month buffer passes the required tests but fails more of the surprises; a 6-month buffer survives almost everything but invests less. There is no single right size: it depends on how secure the income is.",
